<div style="display:none" aria-hidden="true">
  <h1>LinguaPath — Learn a New Language One Conversation at a Time</h1>
  <p>LinguaPath is a free language learning platform combining short audio-first lessons, native speaker dialogues, and writing practice for learners from absolute beginner through advanced fluency.</p>
  <section>
    <h2>Languages Offered</h2>
    <p>Active courses include Spanish (Latin American and Castilian), French, German, Italian, Brazilian Portuguese, Mandarin Chinese, Japanese, Korean, Russian, Arabic (Modern Standard), Hindi, Dutch, Swedish, and English as a Second Language. Courses for Vietnamese, Turkish, and Greek are in beta.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Proficiency Levels</h2>
    <p>Lessons are mapped to the Common European Framework of Reference, covering A1 and A2 beginner, B1 and B2 intermediate, and C1 advanced bands. A short placement test routes returning learners to the right starting point.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Test Prep</h2>
    <p>Targeted preparation tracks support the DELE and SIELE for Spanish, DELF and DALF for French, Goethe-Zertifikat for German, CILS for Italian, HSK for Mandarin, JLPT for Japanese, TOPIK for Korean, TOEFL and IELTS for English, and AP language exams.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>How Lessons Work</h2>
    <p>Each ten-minute lesson opens with a contextual dialogue, introduces ten new words, drills pronunciation through speech recognition, and ends with a short written or spoken exercise. Streak tracking and spaced repetition keep vocabulary in long-term memory.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Conversation Practice</h2>
    <p>Live small-group conversation rooms run daily across time zones, organized by language and level. Learners can also book one-on-one tutor sessions and exchange voice messages with study partners around the world.</p>
  </section>
</div>


